      "problem": "If $\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{-6/5}}={z}^{k},$ then $k=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the radical as a fractional power and then we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{{z}^{-6/5}} & = \\\\ {({z}^{-6/5})}^{1/3} & = \\\\ {z}^{(-6/5)(1/3)} & = \\\\ {z}^{-2/5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $k=-\\frac{2}{5}.$",
